1
00:00:08,181 --> 00:00:11,352
If nothing has an essence,
is anything really there?

2
00:00:12,182 --> 00:00:14,969
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

3
00:00:15,049 --> 00:00:19,240
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and contemplation.

4
00:00:20,072 --> 00:00:21,853
Three parts, one pattern.

5
00:00:21,933 --> 00:00:26,486
An apple, a mountain, and
a bat, a bee and an ant.

6
00:00:26,566 --> 00:00:30,780
A bowl of liquid, a tick at
a pool, and the box of space.

7
00:00:30,860 --> 00:00:35,214
A measured value, two observers,
and a stick in a dark room.

8
00:00:36,033 --> 00:00:39,825
Each time, two ways of
seeing were set side by side.

9
00:00:39,905 --> 00:00:43,697
Undeniably there, given,
measured from its own side.

10
00:00:43,777 --> 00:00:48,589
Or formed, in dependence, designated
together with whoever meets it.

11
00:00:48,669 --> 00:00:50,926
Each time, the formed view held.

12
00:00:51,006 --> 00:00:54,802
By experience, by logic,
and by how things work.

13
00:00:55,621 --> 00:00:59,223
Before the series goes on to
other sides of dependent arising,

14
00:00:59,303 --> 00:01:02,108
I want to stop, and draw some conclusions.

15
00:01:02,921 --> 00:01:05,517
And first, there is a fear to face.

16
00:01:05,597 --> 00:01:08,588
It sits quietly under every part so far.

17
00:01:08,668 --> 00:01:12,247
If it is not faced, everything
else will be heard wrongly.

18
00:01:13,066 --> 00:01:18,204
The fear goes like this. If nothing has
an essence, then nothing is really there.

19
00:01:18,284 --> 00:01:22,257
The world must be hollow.
Ghostly. A kind of void.

20
00:01:22,346 --> 00:01:26,315
Things become dreamlike and
thin. Nothing can really hurt.

21
00:01:26,395 --> 00:01:28,031
And nothing really matters.

22
00:01:28,849 --> 00:01:32,251
Let me set this beside
what happens. Three times.

23
00:01:33,107 --> 00:01:34,363
First, a car.

24
00:01:35,638 --> 00:01:38,996
Surely, if the car has
no essence of its own,

25
00:01:39,076 --> 00:01:41,360
it is only a shape in the mind.

26
00:01:41,440 --> 00:01:43,076
It cannot really touch me.

27
00:01:43,885 --> 00:01:48,592
Or look. I step off the curb without
looking, and the car knocks me down.

28
00:01:49,409 --> 00:01:54,274
The brakes. The speed. The
weight. The road. My not looking.

29
00:01:54,354 --> 00:01:56,965
Conditions meet, and I am on the ground.

30
00:01:57,045 --> 00:01:58,993
No essence was needed for that.

31
00:01:59,818 --> 00:02:02,958
The car was never dangerous
because of a core inside it.

32
00:02:03,038 --> 00:02:05,898
It is dangerous because
of how it meets a body.

33
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:08,374
Second, the rain.

34
00:02:09,282 --> 00:02:14,275
Surely, if the rain is empty, it is
a kind of picture. Nothing gets wet.

35
00:02:15,081 --> 00:02:17,528
Or look. The rain still falls.

36
00:02:17,608 --> 00:02:19,362
The clothes still soak through.

37
00:02:19,442 --> 00:02:22,786
The river still rises,
and the rice still grows.

38
00:02:22,866 --> 00:02:26,291
Clouds, cold air, the slope of the land.

39
00:02:26,371 --> 00:02:28,823
The rain works exactly as before.

40
00:02:29,683 --> 00:02:31,333
Third, a fever.

41
00:02:32,214 --> 00:02:37,433
Surely, if this body is without
essence, sickness is a sort of illusion.

42
00:02:37,513 --> 00:02:38,810
I can think it away.

43
00:02:39,621 --> 00:02:43,277
Or look. I still catch the
flu. My head still aches.

44
00:02:43,357 --> 00:02:45,206
My temperature still climbs.

45
00:02:45,286 --> 00:02:47,598
And I still need rest, and medicine.

46
00:02:47,678 --> 00:02:52,657
The medicine still works, because it too
meets the body along its own channels.

47
00:02:53,473 --> 00:02:57,795
So without essence, the car still
knocks you down. It still rains.

48
00:02:57,875 --> 00:02:59,253
And you still get sick.

49
00:03:00,053 --> 00:03:01,780
That is the big contrast.

50
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:04,932
The inherent view expects
that without essence,

51
00:03:05,012 --> 00:03:07,840
everything turns ghostly and void.

52
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:11,182
It is just the other way
round. Nothing turns ghostly.

53
00:03:11,262 --> 00:03:16,608
It is all exactly as vivid, as
forceful, and as reliable as it was.

54
00:03:17,409 --> 00:03:20,893
Where does the fear come
from, then? Not from looking.

55
00:03:21,709 --> 00:03:24,971
It is a misunderstanding,
produced by confusion.

56
00:03:25,051 --> 00:03:28,925
By a habitual way of
understanding, of analysing,

57
00:03:29,005 --> 00:03:31,552
and of orienting oneself in the world.

58
00:03:32,369 --> 00:03:36,378
Understanding. The habit links
being real with having a core.

59
00:03:36,458 --> 00:03:39,204
Real is heard as there from its own side.

60
00:03:39,284 --> 00:03:43,910
So when the core is denied,
reality seems to be denied with it.

61
00:03:44,733 --> 00:03:50,087
Analysing. The habit analyses by looking
for what something is made of, underneath.

62
00:03:50,167 --> 00:03:54,367
When analysis finds no core,
it reports: nothing there.

63
00:03:54,447 --> 00:03:56,423
Instead of: nothing missing.

64
00:03:57,241 --> 00:04:02,691
Orienting. The habit stands as a solid me
in here, facing solid things out there.

65
00:04:02,771 --> 00:04:07,555
Take away the solidity of the things, and
that me feels it has lost its footing.

66
00:04:07,635 --> 00:04:09,679
As if the ground had dropped away.

67
00:04:10,506 --> 00:04:13,470
But the force of the car
never came from a core.

68
00:04:13,550 --> 00:04:17,492
Remove the essence, and nothing
is removed from the working.

69
00:04:17,572 --> 00:04:20,431
Because the working never
came from the essence.

70
00:04:21,262 --> 00:04:26,101
The ghostliness is the old view looking
at emptiness through its own glasses.

71
00:04:26,181 --> 00:04:29,851
It sees the floor gone, and
expects the room to fall.

72
00:04:29,931 --> 00:04:32,287
The room was never standing on that floor.

73
00:04:33,098 --> 00:04:37,026
This is why I call it a
misunderstanding, not a discovery.

74
00:04:37,106 --> 00:04:40,464
Nihilism is not the opposite
of the inherent view.

75
00:04:40,544 --> 00:04:42,819
It is the inherent view in mourning.

76
00:04:43,638 --> 00:04:45,777
So what have the first three parts shown?

77
00:04:46,594 --> 00:04:49,232
The given is the default, not the finding.

78
00:04:49,312 --> 00:04:53,715
That things are simply there,
finished, before anything meets them,

79
00:04:53,795 --> 00:04:56,378
is how they seem before any thought.

80
00:04:56,458 --> 00:04:59,109
When looked for, the self-standing apple,

81
00:04:59,189 --> 00:05:04,340
the neutral liquid, and the value standing
before any measurement are never found.

82
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:05,620
They are supplied.

83
00:05:06,409 --> 00:05:08,000
What appears is formed.

84
00:05:08,080 --> 00:05:12,660
The thing met, the one who meets it, and
the channel of meeting are designated

85
00:05:12,740 --> 00:05:16,374
together. None is the finished
layer under the others.

86
00:05:17,189 --> 00:05:18,997
Agreement needs no floor.

87
00:05:19,077 --> 00:05:22,149
Beings of one kind agree,
and correct each other,

88
00:05:22,229 --> 00:05:23,916
along shared channels.

89
00:05:23,996 --> 00:05:27,548
Observers agree by interacting,
and checking again.

90
00:05:28,353 --> 00:05:30,134
No new floor, either.

91
00:05:30,214 --> 00:05:33,164
Not the mind, holding the world inside it.

92
00:05:33,244 --> 00:05:36,371
Not relations, as the
true stuff underneath.

93
00:05:36,451 --> 00:05:41,266
Each time the floor was moved, it
was the same habit, in a new place.

94
00:05:42,085 --> 00:05:45,361
Nothing that works is lost.
The apple is still eaten.

95
00:05:45,441 --> 00:05:47,086
The water is still drunk.

96
00:05:47,166 --> 00:05:49,274
The experiment is still repeated.

97
00:05:49,354 --> 00:05:53,096
What fails is only the extra
claim: from its own side.

98
00:05:53,910 --> 00:05:57,811
And now a fourth. Without
essence, nothing turns ghostly.

99
00:05:57,891 --> 00:06:02,200
The car, the rain and the fever
are exactly as real as they were.

100
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:05,121
What goes is only the
floor that was never there,

101
00:06:05,201 --> 00:06:07,626
and the fear that grew from imagining it.

102
00:06:08,458 --> 00:06:11,073
One last time in this section, the test.

103
00:06:11,894 --> 00:06:16,189
By experience. In four parts,
an essence was never met.

104
00:06:16,269 --> 00:06:19,369
Not in the apple, the
bowl or the electron.

105
00:06:19,449 --> 00:06:21,543
And not in the car that knocks me down.

106
00:06:21,623 --> 00:06:24,545
What was met was always
the appearing itself.

107
00:06:24,625 --> 00:06:28,653
Vivid, exact, and found
only in its conditions.

108
00:06:29,466 --> 00:06:34,604
By logic. Anything put forward as
standing on its own has to be picked out.

109
00:06:34,684 --> 00:06:36,750
And picking it out makes it dependent.

110
00:06:36,830 --> 00:06:42,830
A thing, a mind, a relation: each
undoes itself the moment it is named.

111
00:06:43,067 --> 00:06:45,799
And the ghostly void is no better off.

112
00:06:45,879 --> 00:06:49,241
Nothing is really there still
pictures a there that has gone empty.

113
00:06:50,062 --> 00:06:53,773
By working. The car knocks
you down. The rain falls.

114
00:06:53,853 --> 00:06:56,667
The fever rises, and the medicine works.

115
00:06:56,747 --> 00:07:00,893
An essence could not do any of this,
because what is fixed cannot meet

116
00:07:00,973 --> 00:07:03,859
anything. Dependence explains all of it.

117
00:07:04,669 --> 00:07:09,792
So the given, the inherent, is not
the truer view. It is the default one.

118
00:07:09,872 --> 00:07:13,207
And the ghostly void it
fears is its own shadow.

119
00:07:14,009 --> 00:07:17,325
I want to say plainly why I
keep using these examples.

120
00:07:17,405 --> 00:07:21,904
An apple tossed from hand to hand.
A mountain. A bowl of liquid.

121
00:07:21,984 --> 00:07:24,785
A tick at a pool. A click in a laboratory.

122
00:07:24,865 --> 00:07:27,574
A car, the rain, a fever.

123
00:07:28,402 --> 00:07:30,863
They are not decorations for an argument.

124
00:07:30,943 --> 00:07:33,771
The whole purpose is to
correct a misconception,

125
00:07:33,851 --> 00:07:35,528
and to do it with impact.

126
00:07:36,350 --> 00:07:39,585
The misconception does
not live in our theories.

127
00:07:39,665 --> 00:07:45,523
It lives in how the apple feels in the
hand. There. Finished. From its own side.

128
00:07:45,603 --> 00:07:48,734
An argument alone rarely reaches that far.

129
00:07:49,554 --> 00:07:52,559
So I put the two ways
of seeing side by side,

130
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:55,969
as sharply as I can, with
things everyone has held,

131
00:07:56,049 --> 00:07:59,270
climbed, drunk, or been knocked down by.

132
00:07:59,350 --> 00:08:02,753
The contrast has to be
felt, not only followed.

133
00:08:03,561 --> 00:08:06,769
I know it is not easy to
turn around and see this.

134
00:08:06,849 --> 00:08:09,051
The habit is older than any thought.

135
00:08:09,131 --> 00:08:12,181
And it returns the moment
attention is off duty.

136
00:08:13,010 --> 00:08:15,702
The first response is usually rejection.

137
00:08:15,782 --> 00:08:17,781
Surely the apple is just there.

138
00:08:17,861 --> 00:08:22,047
Surely without essence it must
all be ghostly. That is natural.

139
00:08:22,127 --> 00:08:26,467
I do not expect one reading,
or one video, to undo it.

140
00:08:27,294 --> 00:08:28,573
But it is gradual.

141
00:08:28,653 --> 00:08:33,727
Each time the old picture is set beside
what is actually met, it loosens a little.

142
00:08:34,533 --> 00:08:37,754
What first seems counter-intuitive
starts to make sense.

143
00:08:37,834 --> 00:08:40,037
What makes sense starts to look logical.

144
00:08:40,117 --> 00:08:44,004
And in the end, it is the
old view that looks strange.

145
00:08:44,084 --> 00:08:46,858
And the dependent view
that is simply tenable.

146
00:08:46,938 --> 00:08:50,680
The only way the apple, the car
and the rain could work at all.

147
00:08:51,545 --> 00:08:53,562
From rejection to acceptance.

148
00:08:53,651 --> 00:08:57,498
From counter-intuitive, to
highly logical and tenable.

149
00:08:57,578 --> 00:08:59,962
That is the turn these examples are for.

150
00:09:00,773 --> 00:09:03,926
This is Part 4 of the
Dependent Arising series,

151
00:09:04,006 --> 00:09:06,118
and the close of its first section.

152
00:09:06,921 --> 00:09:11,406
Next, the series turns to other
major sides of dependent arising.

153
00:09:11,486 --> 00:09:14,042
What is a phenomenon? Mind and matter.

154
00:09:14,122 --> 00:09:16,071
And the logic of dependency.

155
00:09:16,885 --> 00:09:21,900
What is left when essence goes is not
less than before. It is exactly this.

156
00:09:21,980 --> 00:09:26,021
Vivid and working, with nothing
behind it, and nothing missing.

